    {
      "id": "term-eng-t194",
      "termNumber": "194",
      "engSourceId": "eng-t194-v1",
      "title": "offering",
      "sourceFile": "eng/json/015.content.json",
      "selectedBy": "passage",
      "text": {
        "status": "source",
        "sourceId": "eng-t194-v1",
        "html": "<p>An <b>offering</b> is a gift or <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t114-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">sacrifice</data> offered in a ritual to God, usually in the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t138-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">temple</data> or on a special <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t3-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">altar</data>. People can make offerings for many reasons, including to give thanks, to be <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t208-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">purified</data>, or to ask <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t53-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">forgiveness</data> for <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t125-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">sin</data>.</p>",
        "textSha256": "9399b752703aaeaf40f2be89a93e979c54cb610e8bc04e96003d39a133494f6f",
        "provenance": {
